  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacities of employers&apos; and workers&apos; organizations to participate effectively in the development of social and labour policy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support provided for employers and workers&apos; organizations in the garment sector to achieve effective coordination and uphold workers&apos; rights in Jordan&apos;s garment industry and ensure compliance with national labour laws and core international labour standards. The aim is to ensure that employers and workers organizations effectively coordinate to address sector-wide issues.  
 The ILO will support the government and social partners to facilitate the ratification of ILO Occupational Safety and Health Convention, 1981 (No. 155) as well as the Promotional Framework for Occupational Safety and Health Convention, 2006 (No. 187). 
To achieve this, the ILO will be offering support and capacity building to those organization in the national context with a focus on the garment sector in Jordan.
The ILO in Jordan is developing a Decent Work Country Programme for 2025-27 in consultation with the ILO constituents and in alignment with the Government plans and goals. It will also represent the ILO contribution to the United Nations Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework. The DWCP aligns with the Programme and Budget of the ILO for both bienniums, 24-25 and 26-27 and with the ILO Decent Work Agenda and regional plans.</narrative>
  </description>
